It seems that the `entriesOf` function has two overloaded versions, and the compiler is unable to decide which one to use. To resolve this ambiguity, you could explicitly call the desired version of the function by providing a single argument or a pair of arguments.

In this case, you only need a single argument (the expense amount). You can solve this by changing the following line:

```kotlin
chartEntries.value = entriesOf(*expenses.toFloatArray())
```

to

```kotlin
chartEntries.value = entriesOf(*expenses.map { it to 0 }.toTypedArray())
```

This change creates a Pair for each expense amount, setting the second value to 0 (which will be ignored, but resolves the ambiguity issue).

